		{
			dependencies: ["61D0000000000001"]
			description: [
				"&eConduits&r are Ender IO's signature feature: energy, fluid, item and redstone lines that all occupy &lthe same block space&r."
				""
				"&e&lThat is the whole pitch.&r Six conduit types can run through one block, so a wall carrying power, two fluids, items and a redstone signal is one row of blocks rather than five parallel runs."
				""
				"&e&lThe Yeta Wrench configures them&r - right-click a conduit end to cycle insert/extract, crouch-click to hide them inside facades."
				""
				"&7Item conduits take filters and priorities exactly like a sorting system, so a conduit network often replaces a pipe mod entirely.&r"
				""
				"&8Conduit Binder Composite is the crafting base for all of them. Make it in bulk."
			]
			icon: "enderio:energy_conduit"
			id: "4B5FA06D3C9BDCCF"
			rewards: [{
				id: "57BFFE81D0F2BF0B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
